<article class="env-lemma" id="061C">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/061C">Lemma <span data-tag="061C">76.17.5</span>.</a> Same notation and assumptions as in Lemma <a href="/tag/061A" data-tag="061A">76.17.4</a>. We identify sheaves on $X$ and $X'$ via (<a href="/tag/05ZL" data-tag="05ZL">76.9.1.1</a>). There is an action of the sheaf </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  \mathop{\mathcal{H}\! \mathit{om}}\nolimits _{\mathcal{O}_ X}(a^*\Omega _{Y/B}, \mathcal{C}_{X/X'})  \]
</div>
  <p> on the sheaf (<a href="/tag/061B" data-tag="061B">76.17.4.1</a>). Moreover, the action is simply transitive for any object $U'$ of $(X')_{spaces, {\acute{e}tale}}$ over which the sheaf (<a href="/tag/061B" data-tag="061B">76.17.4.1</a>) has a section. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
